<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Saud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1727–</span> · Also known as Al Saud</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Saud is the ruling family of Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, descended from Muhammad bin Saud, who became emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diriyah">Diriyah</a> in 1727. His alliance with the reformer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-abd-al-wahhab">Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab</a> in 1744 created the first Saudi state. After its destruction in 1818 the family founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Nejd</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Ibn Saud</a> created the modern kingdom in 1932.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-saud.jpg" alt="House of Saud" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Coat of arms of Saudi Arabia.svg: SALEM · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Standard_of_Kingdom_of_Saudi_Arabia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
